Optional image fingerprints use pdqhash-python, whose bindings are MIT licensed,
with the separately licensed PDQ implementation from Meta ThreatExchange.
Retain the upstream copyright and license notices when redistributing that code.

Optional media decoding uses PyAV/FFmpeg, Pillow and NumPy. The licensing of
bundled FFmpeg libraries and enabled codecs depends on the distributed builds;
release approval requires reviewing the actual wheels/container artifacts.
Optional PDF support uses pypdfium2/PDFium, not PyMuPDF. PDFium contains its own
third-party notices. Arrow, boto3, warcio, httpx, jsonschema and defusedxml also
retain their respective licenses.

This project does not bundle training datasets or assert rights to any input
content. Generated test fixtures are synthetic. Third-party algorithm names
